1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:09:17,885
Mira: Michael, did you see the new books I bought to trang trí my room? I like to trang trí with classic sách, but you Vietnamese people seem to prefer manga more.

2
00:09:17,935 --> 00:23:54,612
Michael: Your sách are beautiful, Mira. I also like to trang trí my home with sách. But I don't think Vietnamese people only like manga. Many young people now đọc a lot of Vietnamese and world literature. Have you đọc "The Red Number" by Vu Trong Phung yet?

3
00:23:54,662 --> 00:35:51,943
Mira: Haven't đọc it. I'm still... limited in Vietnamese. You know, in Russia, we really value trang trí our homes with sách. Sách aren't just for đọc but also reflect the soul of the homeowner. But I heard you have an entire bookshelf just about politics? That's... special.

4
00:35:51,993 --> 00:43:50,180
Michael: Yeah, I have a bookshelf about politics and history. Every time I go back to America, I bring back a few books. Hey, if you want, I can lend you some English sách about Vietnam so you can understand more about this country. Or... if you'd like, we could go to a bookstore together this weekend? I know a place that sells used sách that are great for trang trí.

5
00:43:50,230 --> 00:53:08,115
Mira: Go with you? I... I don't think that's a good idea. You'll just choose boring political sách. And I don't need anyone's help choosing sách to trang trí my home. I can manage on my own... But... where is this bookstore anyway?

